session Semicontinuous_Analysis = Lower_Semicontinuous +
  description "
    Upper and lower semicontinuity for real-valued functions on a metric
    space: the epsilon-delta calculus, open strict sublevel sets, eventual
    bounds along convergent sequences, attainment on compacta, bounded
    extension off a closed set, the semicontinuous envelopes over the whole
    space and relative to a closed set, scaling of a real infimum, and
    Berge's maximum theorem.  The envelope is the lower semicontinuous hull
    of the Lower_Semicontinuous entry, on which this session is built,
    proved equal to it rather than reproved.
  "
  options [document = pdf, document_output = "output"]
  theories
    Semicontinuity
    Semicontinuous_Envelopes
    Berge
  document_files
    "root.tex"
    "root.bib"
